@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Terms of Trade";
}

<style>
    .trade-page {
        background: #f7f8fa;
        padding: 40px 15px;
        color: #273449;
        font-size: 14px;
        line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .trade-card {
        max-width: 1000px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 35px;
        background: #fff;
        border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
        border-radius: 12px;
        box-shadow: 0 4px 18px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
    }

        .trade-card h1 {
            color: #a84b1b;
            font-size: 30px;
            font-weight: 700;
            margin-bottom: 5px;
        }

    .trade-updated {
        color: #6b7280;
        font-size: 12px;
        margin-bottom: 22px;
    }

    .trade-intro {
        margin-bottom: 25px;
    }

    .trade-step {
        margin-bottom: 24px;
    }

        .trade-step h2 {
            font-size: 18px;
            font-weight: 700;
            color: #17324d;
            margin-bottom: 8px;
        }

        .trade-step p {
            margin-bottom: 8px;
        }

        .trade-step ul {
            padding-left: 24px;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        .trade-step li {
            margin-bottom: 3px;
        }

    .trade-assurance {
        background: #f5f4dc;
        border-left: 4px solid #b5a94b;
        border-radius: 6px;
        padding: 20px;
        margin-top: 30px;
    }

        .trade-assurance h2 {
            font-size: 19px;
            color: #604b16;
            font-weight: 700;
            margin-bottom: 12px;
        }

        .trade-assurance ul {
            padding-left: 22px;
        }

    .trade-quote {
        font-weight: 700;
        color: #8b451b;
        font-style: italic;
        margin-top: 15px;
        margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    @@media (max-width: 576px) {
        .trade-page {
            padding: 20px 10px;
        }

        .trade-card {
            padding: 20px 16px;
        }

            .trade-card h1 {
                font-size: 25px;
            }

        .trade-step h2 {
            font-size: 16px;
        }
    }
</style>

<div class="trade-page">
    <div class="trade-card">

        <h1>Terms of Trade</h1>

        <p class="trade-updated">
            Last updated: October 14, 2026
        </p>

        <p class="trade-intro">
            At Vearium Traders Private Limited, our trade process is
            structured to ensure clarity, compliance, and consistency
            at every stage — from inquiry to final delivery.
        </p>

        <section class="trade-step">
            <h2>Step 1: Buyer Inquiry &amp; Requirement Confirmation</h2>

            <p>Buyer shares product inquiry with specifications such as:</p>

            <ul>
                <li>Commodity type</li>
                <li>Grade / quality parameters</li>
                <li>Quantity</li>
                <li>Packaging requirements</li>
                <li>Delivery terms (Incoterms®)</li>
                <li>Destination port / location</li>
            </ul>

            <p>Our team reviews feasibility and aligns sourcing accordingly.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="trade-step">
            <h2>Step 2: Commercial Offer &amp; Confirmation</h2>

            <p>A formal quotation / offer is issued mentioning:</p>

            <ul>
                <li>Price and currency</li>
                <li>Quality specifications</li>
                <li>Packaging details</li>
                <li>Delivery terms</li>
                <li>Payment terms</li>
                <li>Validity period</li>
            </ul>

            <p>Upon mutual acceptance, order confirmation is executed through:</p>

            <ul>
                <li>Purchase Order (PO)</li>
                <li>Sales Contract / Proforma Invoice</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="trade-step">
            <h2>Step 3: Payment &amp; Contract Compliance</h2>

            <p>
                Payment terms are followed strictly as per agreed conditions
                (advance, LC, or other agreed modes).
            </p>

            <p>
                Trade documentation and regulatory requirements are aligned
                before execution.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="trade-step">
            <h2>Step 4: Procurement &amp; Quality Preparation</h2>

            <p>
                Commodities are procured from approved sources based on
                buyer specifications.
            </p>

            <p>
                Products undergo cleaning, sorting, grading, and lot-wise
                segregation.
            </p>

            <p>Internal quality checks are performed prior to packing.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="trade-step">
            <h2>Step 5: Packing &amp; Pre-Dispatch Verification</h2>

            <p>Goods are packed using suitable, export-grade materials.</p>

            <p>
                Packaging and labeling are verified as per contract and
                destination norms.
            </p>

            <p>
                Pre-dispatch inspection or third-party inspection is
                facilitated where required.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="trade-step">
            <h2>Step 6: Logistics &amp; Shipment Execution</h2>

            <p>
                Logistics arrangements are finalized based on agreed
                Incoterms®.
            </p>

            <p>
                Coordination with transporters, freight forwarders, and
                ports is managed by our logistics team.
            </p>

            <p>Goods are dispatched as per the confirmed shipping schedule.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="trade-step">
            <h2>Step 7: Documentation &amp; Dispatch Intimation</h2>

            <p>
                Shipping and trade documents are prepared accurately,
                including:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>Commercial Invoice</li>
                <li>Packing List</li>
                <li>Transport / Shipping Document</li>
                <li>Certificate of Origin</li>
                <li>Inspection / Quality Certificates (if applicable)</li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                Buyers are informed of dispatch details and document copies
                are shared promptly.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="trade-step">
            <h2>Step 8: Delivery &amp; Buyer Receipt</h2>

            <p>
                Delivery and risk transfer occur as per agreed Incoterms®.
            </p>

            <p>
                Buyer arranges clearance, unloading, and inspection at destination.
            </p>

            <p>Any observations are handled as per contractual terms.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="trade-step">
            <h2>Step 9: Post-Shipment Support</h2>

            <p>
                Continuous coordination for document clarification, trade
                reconciliation, and buyer feedback.
            </p>

            <p>
                Focus remains on long-term relationship and repeat business.
            </p>
        </section>

        <div class="trade-assurance">
            <h2>Our Trade Assurance</h2>

            <ul>
                <li>Transparent communication</li>
                <li>Contractual discipline</li>
                <li>Quality consistency</li>
                <li>Timely execution</li>
            </ul>

            <p class="trade-quote">
                “Structured process. Reliable execution. Trusted outcomes.”
            </p>
        </div>

    </div>
</div>
